WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240
An emergency is an unexpected and serious situation

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.520
where someone needs help right away.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.560
A medical emergency is a specific kind of danger

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:11.080
where a person is so sick or badly hurt

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.600
that they need a doctor or ambulance immediately

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.639
to save their life or prevent serious harm.

00:00:16.639 --> 00:00:18.240
Whatever the situation,

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.480
if you believe it is necessary to call 911,

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.680
then go ahead and make that call.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.639
If it turns out to be a false alarm,

00:00:25.639 --> 00:00:27.480
that is perfectly okay.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.920
It is always better to be cautious and call early

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.000
than to wait until it might be too late.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.599
When you call 911,

00:00:35.599 --> 00:00:38.200
the dispatcher will ask you several questions

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.520
which we will go over shortly.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.279
To make the process easier,

00:00:42.279 --> 00:00:45.360
put your phone on speaker immediately.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.840
This also allows you to follow the dispatcher's instructions

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.959
and provide care while still being able to listen

00:00:51.959 --> 00:00:53.720
and talk to them.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.400
Dispatchers are trained to coach you through CPR

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.240
and other life-saving steps over the phone.

